					],
					"text": "lbj.expo fills a matrix with exponentially distributed random values. tau is the scale (tau = 1/lambda; set either), loc shifts the values, and sym chooses the shape: 1 = exponential upwards from loc, -1 = downwards, 0 = symmetric (Laplace distribution). All take one value per plane, in the units of the matrix type.",
